# Payment Integration Environment Variables Template

## Instructions
1. Copy this file to `.env.local` (do NOT commit to git)
2. Replace PLACEHOLDER values with actual Razorpay credentials
3. Keep this template in version control for reference

# ============================================
# EXISTING VARIABLES (Keep as-is)
# ============================================

PORT=3001
DB_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017/talent-qatar
NODE_ENV=development
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Stream.io configuration
STREAM_API_KEY=your_stream_api_key
STREAM_API_SECRET=your_stream_api_secret

# Inngest configuration
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=your_inngest_event_key
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=your_inngest_signing_key

# Clerk authentication
# (Usually auto-configured by Clerk middleware)

# ============================================
# NEW: RAZORPAY PAYMENT CONFIGURATION
# ============================================

# 🔑 Razorpay API Key ID (Test or Live)
# Get from: Dashboard → Settings → API Keys → Key ID
# Test mode starts with: rzp_test_
# Live mode starts with: rzp_live_
# IMPORTANT: Never commit real credentials!
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=PLACEHOLDER_KEY_ID

# 🔑 Razorpay API Key Secret (Test or Live)
# Get from: Dashboard → Settings → API Keys → Key Secret
# This is sensitive - keep it secret!
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=PLACEHOLDER_KEY_SECRET

# 🔑 Razorpay Webhook Secret
# Get from: Dashboard → Webhooks → Copy Secret
# Used to verify incoming webhook authenticity
# Each webhook configuration has its own secret
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=PLACEHOLDER_WEBHOOK_SECRET

# 🌐 API Base URL
# Used in payment links and webhook callbacks
# Development: http://localhost:3001
# Production: https://api.talent-qatar.com
API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# ============================================
# OPTIONAL: Payment Configuration
# ============================================

# Maximum payment amount in paise (₹10000 = 1000000 paise)
# PAYMENT_MAX_AMOUNT=1000000

# Minimum payment amount in paise (₹100 = 10000 paise)
# PAYMENT_MIN_AMOUNT=10000

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================

# Step 1: Create Razorpay Account (FREE)
# 1. Go to https://razorpay.com/
# 2. Sign up with email
# 3. Email verification
# 4. Complete KYC (for sandbox, this is optional)

# Step 2: Get API Credentials (Test Keys)
# 1. Login to Dashboard: https://dashboard.razorpay.com/
# 2. Navigate to Settings → API Keys
# 3. Under "Test Keys" section, copy:
#    - Key ID → Set as RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
#    - Key Secret → Set as RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET

# Step 3: Get Webhook Secret
# 1. In Dashboard, go to Settings → Webhooks
# 2. Create new webhook with URL: http://localhost:3001/api/payment/webhook
# 3. In webhook settings, copy the Secret
# 4. Set as RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET

# Step 4: Configure Environment
# 1. Create .env.local file in backend directory
# 2. Copy all content from this file
# 3. Replace PLACEHOLDER values with actual keys
# 4. Save file
# 5. Add to .gitignore if not already there

# ============================================
# TESTING WITH SANDBOX CREDENTIALS
# ============================================

# Test Cards (Sandbox Only):
# Success:  4111 1111 1111 1111 (any future date, any CVV)
# Failure:  4111 1111 1111 1112 (any future date, any CVV)
# Auth:     5555 5555 5555 4444 (any future date, any CVV)

# Example test flow:
# 1. npm run dev (backend)
# 2. npm run dev (frontend)
# 3. Create a session
# 4. Try to pay with test card
# 5. Watch backend logs for payment processing

# ============================================
# PRODUCTION MIGRATION
# ============================================

# To go live with real payments:
# 1. Switch to LIVE Mode in Razorpay Dashboard
# 2. Get LIVE credentials (Key ID, Secret)
# 3. Create LIVE webhook and get its secret
# 4. Update .env file with LIVE credentials
# 5. Update API_URL to production domain (https://)
# 6. Test with small real payment first
# 7. Monitor payment success rate
# 8. Set up support process for refunds

# IMPORTANT: Keep test and live credentials in separate .env files!
# - .env.test (test credentials, safe to commit structure)
# - .env.production (LIVE credentials, NEVER commit, use secrets manager)

# ============================================
# SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
# ============================================

# ✅ DO:
# - Store credentials in .env.local or environment variables
# - Use separate test and live keys
# - Rotate keys periodically
# - Monitor API usage in Dashboard
# - Enable 2FA on Razorpay account

# ❌ DON'T:
# - Commit .env files with credentials to git
# - Share credentials via email or chat
# - Use same key for multiple environments
# - Keep credentials in browser/frontend code
# - Log sensitive data

# ============================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================

# Issue: "Invalid API key"
# Solution: Verify RAZORPAY_KEY_ID is correct
#          Check if using test key in test mode

# Issue: "Webhook signature verification failed"
# Solution: Verify RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET is correct
#          In development, signature verification is skipped automatically

# Issue: "Payment order creation failed"
# Solution: Check backend logs for error details
#          Verify API key and secret are correct
#          Ensure database connection is working

# Issue: Payments working locally but not in production
# Solution: Check API_URL matches production domain
#          Verify webhook URL in Razorpay Dashboard
#          Confirm SSL certificate on production server

